  <h2>Reflect: which relationship does each environmental word encode?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the decision path</h3>
    <p>Complete these ideas aloud: <span class="ex">Weather differs from climate because...</span> <span class="ex">Waste becomes pollution when...</span> <span class="ex">An ecosystem includes...</span> <span class="ex">Results from points toward...</span> <span class="ex">Contributes to is useful when...</span> <span class="ex">Mitigation differs from adaptation because...</span> <span class="ex">A proposal becomes easier to evaluate when...</span></p>
    <p>Take one broad statement, such as <span class="ex">The environment is getting worse</span>, and rebuild it. Name the place, time scale, observation, possible cause, effect, evidence source, response, trade-off, and next measure. If the source does not establish a fact, reduce the certainty of the language.</p>
    <p><a href="#next-day-retrieval">Return tomorrow for the five-item retrieval check</a> before rereading the lesson.</p>
  </div>

  <section id="next-day-retrieval" data-lesson-extension="Next-day weather-climate, ecological relationship, evidence strength, response type, and evaluable action retrieval">
    <h2>Next-day retrieval</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <p>Return without rereading the page. Recover the time scale, the ecological relationship, the strength of the evidence, the response purpose, and the measurement needed for a later decision.</p>
    <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You retained weather-climate scale, habitat meaning, cautious evidence language, mitigation-adaptation purpose, and the structure of an evaluable recommendation.">
      <h3>Five delayed checks</h3>
      <div class="quiz-list">
